   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The purpose of a trip",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)러 가다/오다** shows which action is the reason for the trip: 먹다 → **먹으러 가요** (I'm going to eat), 사다 → **사러 가요** (I'm going to buy), 보다 → **보러 가요** (I'm going to see). It is usually used with verbs of movement; the purpose is expressed with this form before 가다/오다."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Form",
     "texto": [
      "After a vowel or **ㄹ** you add **-러**; after another consonant, **-으러**: 사다 → **사러**, 살다 → **살러**, 먹다 → **먹으러**. It is normally used with movement verbs such as 가다 and 오다: 책을 사러 가요 (I'm going to buy a book)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
